    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1084A\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the administrative code of the city of\nNew York, in relation to school bus parking on city streets\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRegulates the parking of school buses operated by or pursuant to a\ncontract with the board of education.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. The administrative code of the city of New York is amended by\nadding a new section 19-610 to read as follows: 3 § 19-608 School bus\nparking on a city street. No school bus operated by or pursuant to a\ncontract with the board of education shall: (a)park on a city street on\nweekdays between the hours of five p.m. and five a.m., or park on a city\nstreet on weekends between the hours of five p.m. on Friday and five\na.m. on Monday.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNew\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn some neighborhoods it has become exceedingly difficult for home\nowners/tenants to find parking on residential streets because these\nspots are being occupied by school buses. Oversized/commercial vehicles\noccupy spaces that should be available to residents. It is the duty of\nschool bus companies operating by or pursuant to a contract with the\nBoard of Education to provide appropriate parking for their vehicles.\nWhile it may be convenient for school bus drivers to park school buses\non streets outside or close to their residence this practice creates\nundue hardships for others.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017/2018: Referred to Cities\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
